-- issue #1253: byte-for-byte the SAME shape as main.mdk, with the ONE flipped
-- variable being the constructor's form -- POSITIONAL (`MkT2 Int`) instead of
-- RECORD (`MkT { fx : Int }`). This is the discriminator the claim rests on:
--
--   medaka check mainpos.mdk
--   -> main.mdk:3:22: Ambiguous constructor: 'MkT2' is brought into scope by
--      both `pa` and `pb`. Import the constructors of only one -- e.g.
--      `import <mod>.{T(..)}` and drop the other's `(..)` -- exit 1
--
-- The R-AMBIGUOUS-CTOR guard (#674/#732) fires correctly HERE. It does not fire
-- for the byte-identical record-form shape in main.mdk. This file is NOT
-- claim.txt's `control:` -- a `control:` must exit 0 (test/must_fail_fixtures/
-- 1092-methodifaceparamsref-bare-name-collision/claim.txt and #1144 document the
-- same harness limitation), and this program's whole discriminating value is
-- that it correctly exits 1. It is kept as a sibling purely as hand-verified
-- documentary evidence; nothing in claim.txt references it.
import pa.{TA2(..), Tag2, tag2}
import pb.{TB2(..)}
main = println (tag2 (MkT2 1))
